STEP 2 — SCREEN DEEP TRACE

CRITICAL RULE: Follow the user's actual experience. Trace each screen the way a user USES it — not as a flat list of elements, but as a journey from what they see first, to what they explore, to what they click into, to what they find deeper.

The rule is: GO DEEP BEFORE GOING WIDE.

When you encounter a tab, a section, or a clickable area — FULLY EXPLAIN everything inside it (every element, table, detail view, and action) BEFORE moving to the next tab or section. Do NOT list all tabs first then go back and explain each one. Enter Tab 1 → explain everything the user sees inside Tab 1 → explain every table inside Tab 1 → explain every row detail inside Tab 1 → explain every action inside Tab 1 → THEN move to Tab 2 and repeat.

