RULES:

GO DEEP BEFORE GOING WIDE. This is the #1 rule. Fully exhaust everything inside a tab, section, table, or detail view BEFORE moving to the next one. Never list all tabs first then go back to explain them. Enter → trace everything inside → leave → next.
The trace order must follow the user's experience: first glance → sections → enter first tab → everything inside that tab (elements, tables, row details, actions) → leave tab → enter next tab → repeat.
Explain EVERY element, not just the "important" ones. The tab that says "Risk" with a badge "1 High, 10 Medium" needs just as much explanation as the main score.
Use plain language. If a technical term appears in the UI, explain what it means the first time you encounter it.
When explaining "where the data comes from," be as specific as possible. Name the API endpoint, the database field, or the calculation logic.
For every number, ask yourself: "If a PM asked me what this number means and why it's that value, could I explain it?" If not, dig deeper.
For every button, ask yourself: "If a new user asked me what happens when I click this, could I walk them through the entire consequence?" If not, trace it further.
Do NOT give high-level summaries. "This dashboard shows project metrics" is USELESS. "This dashboard shows 4 metrics: average model score (quality), model count (scope), iteration count (effort), and source object count (input size) — together they answer the question 'is this project ready for review or does it need more work'" is USEFUL.
CRITICAL FORMATTING RULES:

Each element must be its own section with a blank line before and after it.
Each sub-field (What it shows, What it means, etc.) must be on its own line with the description below it.
Between screens, use a horizontal rule (---) and blank line.
Between tabs, use a horizontal rule (---) and blank line.
Between elements, use a blank line.
NEVER collapse multiple elements into one paragraph.
NEVER skip the "What would be lacking without it" field.
NEVER list multiple tabs then go back — enter each tab, fully trace it, leave, then next tab.
